<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 49,840 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 49,840 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 49,840 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Tuesday compared to 41,710 tonnes in the same period on Monday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Tuesday     May 26</p>
<p>    Export cargo		12,181	25,480</p>
<p>    Import cargo		37,659	16,230</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and five berthed. In the next 24 hours, nine are expected to sail and nine are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to</p>
<p>unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Gas oil		60,000	 CSP - 10		  27/5</p>
<p>Gas oil		78,000	 Chesa Peak City	 27/5</p>
<p>Vegoil		 18,000	 Ariston		   28/5</p>
<p>Fuel oil	     26,000	 Zoras		     29/5</p>
<p>Fuel oil	     30,000	 Ying Song Hu	    30/5</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
